WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.880
As all Marvel fans know, Groot is a character
who's more about action than he is about talk.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.250
Possessing only a handful of words in his
vocabulary that can be understood by humans,

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:14.050
the tree-like superhero hasn't said much else
other than "I am Groot" and "we are Groot"

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.160
throughout his time in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.700
Of course, each line apparently has a translation.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.260
"I am Groot."

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.140
"Whoa!"

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:21.640
"Language!"

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.260
"Hey!"

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.340
"Wow."

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.600
"Got some acorns on you, kid."

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.080
For example, James Gunn revealed that Groot's
final line to Rocket Raccoon just before crumbling

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:35.320
into space dust in Avengers: Infinity War
translated to, quote, "dad," because that

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.220
ending wasn't sad enough already.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.260
And now, keeping up with what seems like a
new tradition, Marvel gave Groot another intriguing

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.840
final line in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.850
Directors Joe and Anthony Russo revealed what
the talking tree-boy said at the very end

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.450
of Avengers: Endgame when they spoke in a
Q&amp;A session following a screening of the superhero

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.560
ensemble at the Smithsonian National Air and
Space Museum in Washington, D.C.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:03.360
A Reddit user who was in attendance detailed
the Russos' answers to nearly two dozen questions,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.640
one of which regarded Groot and the final
words he uttered in Endgame.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.780
The last place fans saw Groot in Avengers:
Endgame was aboard the spaceship Benatar,

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.000
watching as Star-Lord and Thor have a friendly-but-maybe-not-so-friendly
squabble.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.920
The two heroes exchange some jabs that they
pass off as jokes before Drax the Destroyer

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.380
chimes in and suggests they "fight one another
for the honor of leadership."

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:29.160
After the other Guardians voice their support
for a knife fight, the camera then pans over

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:32.140
to Groot, who smiles and says, "I am Groot."

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:37.220
According to the Russo brothers, that line
genuinely means something: it translates from

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.000
Groot's native language into English as, quote,
"Yes, I like knives."

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.740
So, there you have it: the entire Guardians
of the Galaxy squad wants Star-Lord and Thor

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.000
to settle their differences in a down-and-dirty
knife fight, including little Groot.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.060
"He likes to play with knives.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:53.580
Very well.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.760
We shall indulge him."

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.990
While Groot's final line in Avengers: Endgame
isn't nearly as significant as the last word

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:05.109
he said in Avengers: Infinity War, that doesn't
mean the phrase is completely without meaning

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:06.180
in its own regard.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.539
Groot's last Endgame line leaves things with
the Guardians of the Galaxy on a happy, silly

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.209
note which, in turn, establishes the tone
for the next entry in the team's film trilogy.

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:18.650
Groot joining in on the banter with the rest
of the gang proves that the Guardians are

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:24.480
back in good spirits after Thanos' original
Decimation in 2018 and the reverse-Snap Professor

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.000
Hulk executed in Endgame.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.060
The team may be without Gamora, who got tossed
over a cliff on Vormir so her dad could get

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:31.560
a rock.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.580
But they've finally reassembled and are ready
to locate their missing member.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:40.760
This last sequence for the Guardians in Endgame
teases that they may go on a search for Gamora

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.900
in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, which would
probably benefit from having Thor in tow,

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:50.520
so long as he and Star-Lord can squash the
beef between them… as unlikely as that seems

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.520
at the moment.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:52.580
"You know Thor?"

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.800
"Yeah, tall guy, not that good looking, needed
saving."

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.159
It will be interesting to see how the god
of thunder and the lord of dance get on in

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.260
the third Guardians movie.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.440
Will their apparent rivalry dissipate before
it gets out of hand?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.620
Or will it continue to grow until they have
no choice but to sharpen their knives for

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:14.379
a one-on-one fight, thus satisfying the twisted
wishes of the rest of the team in the process?

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:18.590
Star-Lord may have the advantage of his sweet
dance moves to shimmy and shake around the

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.900
hammer-wielding hero, and knowing Quill, he
might even play by Butch Cassidy rules.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:23.960
"Rules?!

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.100
In a knife fight?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.200
No rules!"

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.280
"Well, if there ain't gonna be any rules,
let's get the fight started.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.920
Somebody count one, two, three, go."

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:31.500
"One, two, three go!"

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.860
On the other hand, Thor is a god who can summon
literal lightning.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.080
If the two were ever to really turn their
verbal stabs into literal ones, Thor would

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.980
probably end up winning you know, as long
as he goes for the head.

